{"agent":"sw-reservedslot","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":4,"detail":"When `reserved_slots`/`reserved_tags` are configured and `plan(parallel=...)` is passed, `_plan.py` sets `p.parallel_line` to `line` already joined with `p.reserved_note`. `Plan.summary` already includes `self.parallel_line`, and this change also appends `self.reserved_note` as a separate summary part. That makes one summary emit the same reserved note twice, e.g. `parallel: 4 (fixed); schedule.reserved_slots: 1` and then later `schedule.reserved_slots: 1` in the same output.","digest":"16f04293a6830d0a","location":"ddflow/core/schedule/_plan.py:p.parallel_line + ddflow/core/schedule/_readiness.py:Plan.summary","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/core/schedule/_plan.py:p.parallel_line + ddflow/core/schedule/_readiness.py:Plan.summary"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"`share` for the regular cap is computed with `len(ordinary)`, where `ordinary` is every non-reserved live item, including worktree leases (line 59 relies on the same list to count `.worktree` items). Worktree leases consume `cfg.worktree.max_parallel`, not the regular `limit`, so they must be excluded when computing the regular ordinary allowance. Example: `cfg.worktree.enabled=True`, `limit=4`, `cfg.schedule.reserved_slots=2`, one live ordinary worktree item, and no regular live items. The regular cap should still allow `ordinary_free(4, 2, 0)=2` ordinary flight tasks, but `len(ordinary)=1` gives `share=1`; with two worktree items `share=0`. The returned `Slots(..., min(share, flight), ...)` then caps the normal cut at 0/1 instead of 2, starving ordinary features the reservation rule says may run.","digest":"d75d8ce51a15eae8","location":"ddflow/core/schedule/_reserved.py:56","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/core/schedule/_reserved.py:56"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"<ddflow-record kind=\"rule\" id=\"r-task-phase-needs-wave\" by=\"[REDACTED:hostname]-ddflow-7267fe\" trust=\"agent\">Every task has a phase, stated dependencies and a wave tag: RULE: every task names the phase whose progress it counts towards, states its dependencies in needs, and carries a wave:N tag (ddflow waves --stamp derives it). A task with no prerequisite carries the tag no-deps, so that none is a decision and not an omission. Work that blocks a phase belongs in that phase; a catch-all such as bugs-2 is only for work no phase serves. This covers tasks ddflow files itself, including bug fix tasks. CHECK: a task inherits the needs of its phase, so read the phase needs before placing a task; a wrong …</ddflow-record>\nThe newly added test file `tests/test_reserved_slots.py` implements test helper functions like `_task` that add tasks to logs without including a wave tag or explicit `needs` dependencies/`no-deps` tags, violating the rule [r-task-phase-needs-wave] which mandates that every task carries a wave:N tag or a no-deps tag and states dependencies in needs.","digest":"18c0b3864c1dace5","location":"tests/test_reserved_slots.py:16","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_reserved_slots.py:16"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`open_slots` treats every non-reserved live lease as consuming the parallel cap (`ordinary_free(limit, wanted, len(ordinary))`), but a worktree lease does not count against that cap. With limit 2, `reserved_slots` 1 (ordinary may hold 1), and one ordinary worktree task already leased, `flight` is still 2 while `share` becomes `ordinary_free(2, 1, 1) = 0`, so the offer hands out no ordinary parallel slot even though parallel occupancy is 0. The same count is used by `idle_reserved` via `_flying` (every live lease): limit 4, `reserved_slots` 2, two ordinary worktree tasks and nothing on the parallel limit yields `ordinary_free == 0` and `idle == 2`, so `binding` is `2 + 2 >= 4` and the adaptive limit grows though no parallel slot is in use.","digest":"8f88680b3014cc0a","location":"ddflow/core/schedule/_reserved.py:57","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/core/schedule/_reserved.py:57"}],"chunks_total":7,"coverage":"7/7 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":42079,"diff_sha":"3d98e6b068b8fe14fd275d0f90ff6c0eb2af18012dade5905d86e200db37acfd","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1019.0,"excluded_bytes":4330,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"deepseek","findings":4,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"976d8ccb2d0f5bf4","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DX-reserved-slot.critic.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261105T130422Z-1735edf9.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7],"reviewed_head":"b7f2a17f8c21f7907323d078dd190585fd562139","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 421833bff13cf62d2adf1cda235b18b48b647680","ddflow/adapters/fakes/optimizer.py":"100644 22f9a1fb6ae19e80325270d829662e3192248820","ddflow/adapters/optimizer.py":"100644 643894db5e58383e79e198ebe74deab39b5499ed","ddflow/config_sections/schedule.py":"100644 21c65edc266ab1bef891b70a980b865674336c76","ddflow/core/schedule/__init__.py":"100644 f7c1ddd03076f5da091ed5dac6d755698ee6e8ab","ddflow/core/schedule/_plan.py":"100644 fdc9a3d3b16886adc12801ac57518f01fbc37780","ddflow/core/schedule/_readiness.py":"100644 ae8fef270a95646b22e1987b888a5550155cb3ec","ddflow/core/schedule/_reserved.py":"100644 8dd839f0eeb61103a078b6117b4609b5af7698c4","ddflow/services/flowstate.py":"100644 20ec0c4530bedc82da73d77f326b655576c29392","ddflow/templates/prompts/help/parallel.md":"100644 f4cb1b236db5305dc8bd341749363914b34b1287","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.schedule.reserved_slots.toml":"100644 510bbb7250436e76b3a4873108dfbe36ddcbeb48","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.schedule.reserved_tags.toml":"100644 0cebb65d7385f8667cde01a83bcfaf82c9147c33","tests/test_reserved_slots.py":"100644 3542966568f30632cc95cd347f65d23f8040082f"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-